**What I implemented:** `translate(text)` splits the sentence, translates each word via `_translate_word`, and rejoins. Each word: (1) vowel/`xr`/`yt` start → append `ay`; (2) `[^aeiou]*qu` prefix → move to end + `ay`; (3) consonant cluster before `y` → move to end + `ay`; (4) plain consonant cluster → move to end + `ay`. Rule order is essential (`rhythm` fails under plain-consonant matching). **Verified by:** RED run on the stub (0/22, `None` returns), GREEN run (22/22 pass on the standard Exercism pig-latin cases), `py_compile` syntax check, and a fresh import run on the final tree — all evidence on disk.
